      "severity": "must",
      "text": "`reordered_conjunction` binds the right script with `hi lo`, so it states `id > lo AND id < hi` ~ `id < lo AND id > hi`, which is false (for `lo = 0`, `hi = 3` on `items` the left returns rows 1 and 2 and the right returns none), so `sql_run` cannot close it and the test of the conjunction normalizer cannot pass as written. Fix: bind the right script with `lo hi`, so that both sides state the same range and differ only in clause order and repetition."
